# I04.var09 root publication wrappers v100 — static NO_GO

This is a static, pre-execution finding. The three preserved read-only root methods are `tmp/i04-var09-root-catalog-stage-v100-20261008.py` (5,866 bytes/SHA-256 `8c88d7649c10d39780891c4d93953c50f3105203746a0a4796d2b642889ab239`), `tmp/i04-var09-root-publication-byte-audit-v100-20261008.py` (8,397 bytes/SHA-256 `ee293d78d04a5dc32d695dcce6cf6a79713ce5c913770b381880c44427a638bb`), and `tmp/i04-var09-root-publication-capture-v100-20261008.py` (5,144 bytes/SHA-256 `1dc7222ee6669df061f276cc222a80d08f75198957f6a9c7061055b32b7e0ad6`). No catalog, Git, native, or publisher execution was performed under them.

The canonical owned archives being constructed are `cases/simlox-air-support/I04-var09-arrived-system-next-mission-v1.0.0/preserved-context/owned-catalog-local-498.json.bytes` and `owned-catalog-git-498.json.bytes`. The v100 catalog-stage method instead names `preserved-context/catalog-local-498.json.bytes`; its byte auditor names case-root `catalog-local-498.json.bytes` and `catalog-git-498.json.bytes`. Both paths disagree with actual custody. The byte auditor must also derive and enforce the 403 accepted parent disk/Git path identities as the exact set of 401 parent evidence-index source paths plus parent `evidence-index.json` and `review/independent-content-go-2026-10-08.md`, rather than accepting a count alone.

Decision: `NO_GO_PUBLICATION_WRAPPERS_V100`. Preserve these exact methods as inert history and review distinct corrected wrappers before any catalog append or Git stage. The independent classifier and self-check remain mutable drafts; their early local failures were tool-decoded diagnostics only and are not original binary captures.
